# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS
# Two sources require this section:
#   - Game rulebook rules 39-40 (docs/RULES.md): never push secrets or
#     credentials, even to a private repo shared only with the lecturer.
#     Sanction: severe security failure and project failure.
#   - Engineering standard §7.4 (docs/SEGAL_GUIDELINES.md): .gitignore MUST
#     include .env, *.key, *.pem, credentials.json. Checked by automatic scan.
# These entries exist BEFORE the OAuth code does. Do not remove them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
*.key
*.pem

# .env-example carries dummy values and MUST be committed (§7.4)
!.env-example

client_secret*.json
token.json
token.pickle
*.token
secrets/
.secrets/
*_secret*
*-secret*

# Nonces must stay secret until end of game (rule 18) — never commit live ones
nonces/
*.nonce

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project runtime artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained Q-tables can be large; commit deliberately, not by accident
*.qtable
models/checkpoints/

# Local run output. NOTE: the four required JSON artifacts
# (declaration_/config_/log_/result_) MUST be committed per rule 50 and
# Appendix F rule 4 — keep them out of this ignore list.
logs/
*.log
runs/
tmp/

# Tunnel config may embed auth tokens
ngrok.yml
ngrok.yaml
.localtonet/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source specification PDFs — copyrighted course material
# Rule 49 requires both submission repos to be PUBLIC. These PDFs are
# (c) Dr. Yoram Segal and are not ours to redistribute. They stay on disk as
# the local source of truth; the translated extracts in docs/ are committed
# instead. Remove these two lines only if the lecturer authorises publishing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
police_thief_p2p.pdf
software_submission_guidelines-V3.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Knowledge graph (graphify)
# graph.json and graph.html are ~2 MB each and are regenerable at zero API cost
# with `graphify update .`. Committing them would multiply the size of .git on
# every refresh and produce diffs no human can read. Only GRAPH_REPORT.md
# (~68 KB markdown) is committed, so a fresh clone — and the grader — still gets
# the navigable map. See CLAUDE.md "Knowledge graph (graphify)".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphify-out/
.planning/graphs/graph.json
.planning/graphs/graph.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent harness config
# .claude/settings.json IS committed — it carries the SessionStart graph hook
# that every agent depends on. Everything else under .claude/ is per-machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.codex/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
